WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:02.370
- Let's close out with one
last story to warm your heart.

00:00:02.370 --> 00:00:04.125
This is What I'm Liking.

00:00:04.125 --> 00:00:06.950
(jazzy music begins)
(audience applauds)

00:00:06.950 --> 00:00:09.720
March is women's history
month, making it a great time

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:12.430
to celebrate female first's
across this country.

00:00:12.430 --> 00:00:14.810
That's why I wanna tell
you about Emily Harrington.

00:00:14.810 --> 00:00:16.660
Not long ago, she became the first woman

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:18.970
to free climb the golden gate route

00:00:18.970 --> 00:00:21.870
of El Capitan in under 24 hours.

00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:24.230
I couldn't do it in 24 years.

00:00:24.230 --> 00:00:26.380
Cool.
(audience laughs)

00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:28.490
This is a serious feat, people.

00:00:28.490 --> 00:00:31.370
She scaled nearly... it's
the nearly perpendicular

00:00:31.370 --> 00:00:33.720
3,200 foot rock face in Yosemite

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:36.016
in 21 hours and 14 minutes.

00:00:36.016 --> 00:00:37.140
(audience claps)
What?

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:40.280
With just a rope for safety.

00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:43.820
I'd need a helicopter to fly me there.

00:00:43.820 --> 00:00:45.740
We have Emily on the line right now.

00:00:45.740 --> 00:00:47.294
What's up Emily?

00:00:47.294 --> 00:00:48.127
(audience applauds)

00:00:48.127 --> 00:00:49.600
- Hey there, how are you?

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:53.270
- You are so impressive,
I'm gonna lead with that.

00:00:53.270 --> 00:00:55.900
I mean, you pulled off
just such an insane thing.

00:00:55.900 --> 00:00:57.840
Has this been a dream of yours?

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:00.480
- Yes, I've been climbing
since I was 10 years old.

00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:02.690
Everything from climbing competitions

00:01:02.690 --> 00:01:04.220
to climbing Mount Everest

00:01:04.220 --> 00:01:07.740
but this goal in particular
really challenged me

00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:11.300
in the most inspiring and difficult way.

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:15.270
I spent years practicing and
training to get to this point.

00:01:15.270 --> 00:01:17.550
When you climb El Cap, El Capitan,

00:01:17.550 --> 00:01:19.130
the hardest part is
actually at the very end.

00:01:19.130 --> 00:01:22.010
So I like to tell people that
it's like running a marathon

00:01:22.010 --> 00:01:24.390
and then running your
fastest hundred meters

00:01:24.390 --> 00:01:25.470
at the very, very end.

00:01:25.470 --> 00:01:28.940
So it presents this huge
endurance challenge.

00:01:28.940 --> 00:01:32.210
During a previous attempt, I
actually had a really bad fall.

00:01:32.210 --> 00:01:34.611
I wound up in the hospital
with a concussion.

00:01:34.611 --> 00:01:36.470
So there's a lot of failure and struggle

00:01:36.470 --> 00:01:39.197
but eventually I was successful.

00:01:39.197 --> 00:01:40.943
(audience claps)
- Oh my gosh.

00:01:41.930 --> 00:01:44.410
So I mean, I can only imagine

00:01:44.410 --> 00:01:46.000
but how did you feel when you said,

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:48.710
it's a historic record you
just said, how did that feel?

00:01:48.710 --> 00:01:49.760
- I think it was...

00:01:49.760 --> 00:01:52.180
it was more a combination
of relief and joy

00:01:52.180 --> 00:01:54.070
but there was also this sadness

00:01:54.070 --> 00:01:56.460
and realizing that this process was over.

00:01:56.460 --> 00:01:58.900
I mean, I spent years
focused on this one thing

00:01:58.900 --> 00:02:01.200
and then all of a sudden, it was finished.

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:04.430
But honestly, you know, it's
just one part of my career.

00:02:04.430 --> 00:02:06.640
I feel like I have a lot more to come.

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:10.210
I'm really excited to try
other routes on El Capitan

00:02:10.210 --> 00:02:12.140
as well as travel the world

00:02:12.140 --> 00:02:14.510
and continue to climb
things that inspire me.

00:02:14.510 --> 00:02:16.450
- I was gonna say like,
what's your next thing?

00:02:16.450 --> 00:02:18.640
Do you have, what would
you like to do next?

00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:20.957
Do you know yet or are you
still thinking about it?

00:02:20.957 --> 00:02:22.860
- I'm still thinking about
it at, it's up in the air.

00:02:22.860 --> 00:02:26.540
There's a lot harder
routes on El Cap itself

00:02:26.540 --> 00:02:28.440
and then there's big
walls all over the world.

00:02:28.440 --> 00:02:30.175
I actually just went to Kurdistan

00:02:30.175 --> 00:02:32.060
and climbed a big wall there.

00:02:32.060 --> 00:02:33.590
I'm going to Baffin Island,

00:02:33.590 --> 00:02:36.130
which is up near the Arctic circle.

00:02:36.130 --> 00:02:38.470
So there's quite a bit to do.

00:02:38.470 --> 00:02:40.300
- I love that your like, hobby and passion

00:02:40.300 --> 00:02:41.680
takes you to so many cool places

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:43.694
that you might have
never visited otherwise,

00:02:43.694 --> 00:02:44.810
that's really cool.

00:02:44.810 --> 00:02:47.010
I'm liking your post right now, Emily.

00:02:47.010 --> 00:02:48.650
We think you're awesome

00:02:48.650 --> 00:02:51.140
and that's not... you look like a warrior!

00:02:51.140 --> 00:02:54.020
I mean, you just look
badass, let's just be real.

00:02:54.020 --> 00:02:56.390
That's not all though, our
season long partner Pilot Pen,

00:02:56.390 --> 00:02:58.890
makers of G2, the go-to pen
of the Kelly Clarkson Show,

00:02:58.890 --> 00:03:00.890
want to honor ultimate overachievers.

00:03:00.890 --> 00:03:02.850
I can't imagine anyone that deserves this

00:03:02.850 --> 00:03:05.410
more than you right now in this moment.

00:03:05.410 --> 00:03:06.660
So they're gonna be writing you a check

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:08.245
for a thousand dollars, how's that sound?

00:03:08.245 --> 00:03:09.506
(audience applauds)

00:03:09.506 --> 00:03:11.730
- Wow, thank you!
(Kelly laughs)

00:03:11.730 --> 00:03:13.320
- [Kelly] Thank you so much, Emily!

00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:14.983
Good luck on your next climb.

